# Keep line endings deterministic for files whose consumers care about them.
#
# Added 2026-11-11 after the F-Droid submission failed three CI runs. Git on
# Windows checks files out with CRLF by default, and copying from a browser adds
# CRLF to the clipboard regardless of what the page contained. fdroiddata's CI
# runs `fdroid rewritemeta`, which normalises metadata to LF and then fails if
# the file changed -- so a CRLF copy produces a diff on every single line and
# the job fails no matter how correct the content is. Their contribution
# template states the requirement plainly: "Metadata must use LF as line
# ending."
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf

# Shell scripts and Gradle wrappers break outright with CRLF: a `#!/bin/sh`
# line ending in \r makes the kernel look for an interpreter named "sh\r".
*.sh text eol=lf
gradlew text eol=lf

# Binary, never touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.jks binary
*.aar binary
*.jar binary
*.keystore binary
